  "comments": "The standard weight of these coins was 10/11 troy ounce (436.4 grains); alloy composition - Ag 50%, Cu 40%, Ni 5%, Zn 5%.<br /><br />\r\nThis coin was not included in demonetization legislation when decimalization was introduced in 1971. It has been confirmed by the Royal Mint that the coin remains legal tender, having been remonetized with a value of 25 pence.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Varieties:</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Sp#4078</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">(1937)</span> Coronation commemorative crown, regular strike;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Sp#4079</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">(1937)</span> Similar, Proof <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">FDC</span>;<br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Sp#4079</span> <span style=\"font-style:italic;\">(1937)</span> Similar, Frosted VIP Proof;",
